(6t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)\\, \\\\ \\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6t)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6t)\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372699 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372700 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372699 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186445554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372699 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372699 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372699 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186445554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372699 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "2d23240b-1c76-53c1-a74c-bff1d5b80be5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372700 #edb/ref 1080 "-2\\operatorname{sin}(6t)+3\\operatorname{cos}(6t)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372700 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372700 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fd3a65fc-4bf8-52f4-ad48-b1d77f53af91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372701 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372702 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372701 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186445593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372701 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372701 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372701 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186445593 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372701 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "cc61ae92-49a5-5ac1-a97b-53dc0941e692" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372702 #edb/ref 1080 "-2\\operatorname{cos}(6t)-3\\operatorname{sin}(6t)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372702 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186372702 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "573d9cac-76d3-5ac7-8c30-2adbdb95893b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396993 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396993 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396993 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186397002 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396993 #edb/ref 1069 "q-337121" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396993 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396993 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,c$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $x({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})\\,$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ can be obtained by {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by {{field-3}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396993 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0d9118b1-b0ff-5db4-a05c-ec3ad938a6f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396993 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L4}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Starting from $\\text{L4},$\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwe multiply both sides on the left by $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}$ to get\n\n$$\n({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L5}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides on the left by }({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L7}.$ Using line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,c.\n$$\n\nFrom line $\\text{L6}$, we know that $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}).$ Substituting this expression for $c$ into the formula for $x(t)$ gives\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L7}.$ Thus, line $\\text{L7}$ can be obtained by $\\text{substituting }c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\text{ into }x(t)={e}^{At}c.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L7}$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Since $At$ and $-A{t}_{0}$ commute, we can use the property \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into line $\\text{L7},$ we get line $\\text{L8}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by the fact that ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}\\text{ when }X\\text{ and }Y\\text{ commute}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396994 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396994 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396994 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396994 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396994 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396994 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186396997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396994 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4034d58e-9aa0-5353-8a0b-15f70b5c05f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396995 #edb/ref 1080 "evaluating $x(t)={e}^{At}c$ at $t={t}_{0}$ and solving for $c$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396995 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396995 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "04e051ba-0925-5595-906b-3d9455a124a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396996 #edb/ref 1080 "left-multiplying $x(t)={e}^{At}c$ by ${e}^{-At}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396996 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396996 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d66a48e